  "finalText": "I built the 6 s chart at 1920×1080, and a contact sheet of the sequence shows the order working as intended. I haven't run the critic or played it back in real time.\n\n- **Intro:** The title **Revenue by quarter** sits top-left in dark navy with a grey \"$M\" subline. Both slide up and fade in.\n- **Axis:** The baseline draws on left to right from 0.4 s, with the Q1–Q4 labels fading in underneath.\n- **Bars:** They grow up from the baseline one after another at about 0.35 s intervals (Q1 at 1.3 s, Q4 at 2.35 s). Each has rounded top corners and the heights are in proportion to 12, 18, 15 and 27.\n- **Value labels:** Each value fades in and rises just above its bar once the bar has grown. The numbers fade in rather than count up.\n- **Q4:** The bar grows, overshoots slightly, settles, and turns from slate blue to coral (`#F25C54`). Its \"27\" is larger and bolder, in the same coral, and arrives with a Back Out pop.\n\nI wrote the subline as \"$M\" because the brief gave the unit but no year.\n\nIf you want, I can make the numbers count up, add faint gridlines, or add a gentle looping glow on the Q4 bar."
